{"path":"named_req/ReversibleContainer","title":"C++ named requirements: ReversibleContainer","titleHtml":"<span class=\"t-title-prefix\">C++ named requirements:</span><em class=\"t-named-req\">ReversibleContainer</em>","originalUrl":"https://en.cppreference.com/w/cpp/named_req/ReversibleContainer","section":"named_req","kind":"page","summary":"A ReversibleContainer is a Container that has iterators that meet the requirements of either LegacyBidirectionalIterator or LegacyRandomAccessIterator.","html":"<p>A <strong class=\"selflink\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">ReversibleContainer</em></strong> is a <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/Container\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">Container</em></a> that has iterators that meet the requirements of either <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/BidirectionalIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyBidirectionalIterator</em></a> or <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/RandomAccessIterator\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">LegacyRandomAccessIterator</em></a>.  Such iterators allow a <em class=\"t-named-req\">ReversibleContainer</em> to be iterated over in reverse.\n</p>\n<h3 id=\"Requirements\">Requirements</h3>\n<p>A type satisfies <em class=\"t-named-req\">ReversibleContainer</em> if it satisfies <a href=\"/w/cpp/named_req/Container\"><em class=\"t-named-req\">Container</em></a>, its iterator type belongs to the bidirectional or random access <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator\">iterator categories</a> and, given the following types and values, the semantic and complexity requirements in the tables below are satisfied:\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Type\n</td>\n<td> Definition\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>X</code>\n</td>\n<td> an <em class=\"t-named-req\">ReversibleContainer</em> type\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code>T</code>\n</td>\n<td> the <code>value_type</code> of <code>X</code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc-hitem\">\n<td> Value\n</td>\n<td> Definition\n</td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td> <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code>\n</td>\n<td> a value of type <code>X</code>\n</td></tr>\n</table>\n<h4 id=\"Types\">Types</h4>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tr>\n<th>Name\n</th>\n<th>Type\n</th>\n<th>Requirements\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> X<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">reverse_iterator</span></span>\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/reverse_iterator\"><span class=\"kw663\">std::<span class=\"me2\">reverse_iterator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>X<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">iterator</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span>\n</td>\n<td>an iterator type whose <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator\">value type</a> is <code>T</code>\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> X<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">const_reverse_iterator</span></span>&nbsp;\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator/reverse_iterator\"><span class=\"kw663\">std::<span class=\"me2\">reverse_iterator</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span>X<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">const_iterator</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span></span>&nbsp;\n</td>\n<td>a constant iterator type whose <a href=\"/w/cpp/iterator\">value type</a> is <code>T</code>\n</td></tr></table>\n<h4 id=\"Expressions\">Expressions</h4>\n<p>The types <code>reverse_iterator</code> and <code>const_reverse_iterator</code> in the following table denote <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> X<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">reverse_iterator</span></span> and <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> X<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">const_reverse_iterator</span></span> respectively.\n</p>\n<table class=\"wikitable\">\n<tr>\n<th>Expression\n</th>\n<th>Type\n</th>\n<th>Semantics\n</th>\n<th>&nbsp;Complexity&nbsp;\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a.<span class=\"me1\">rbegin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code>reverse_iterator</code><br><code>const_reverse_iterator</code> for constant <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">reverse_iterator<span class=\"br0\">(</span>a.<span class=\"me1\">end</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td>Constant\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a.<span class=\"me1\">rend</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code>reverse_iterator</code><br><code>const_reverse_iterator</code> for constant <code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a</span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">reverse_iterator<span class=\"br0\">(</span>a.<span class=\"me1\">begin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td>Constant\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a.<span class=\"me1\">crbegin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code>const_reverse_iterator</code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">const_cast</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> X<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>a<span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">rbegin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td>Constant\n</td></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\">a.<span class=\"me1\">crend</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td><code>const_reverse_iterator</code>\n</td>\n<td><code class=\"t-c\"><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">const_cast</span><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> X<span class=\"sy3\">&amp;</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span>a<span class=\"br0\">)</span>.<span class=\"me1\">rend</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span></span></code>\n</td>\n<td>Constant\n</td></tr></table>\n<h3 id=\"Library_types\">Library types</h3>\n<p>The following standard library types satisfy <em class=\"t-named-req\">ReversibleContainer</em> requirements:\n</p>\n<table class=\"t-dsc-begin\">\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/array\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>array</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx11\">(C++11)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  fixed-sized inplace contiguous array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/deque\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>deque</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  double-ended queue <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/list\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>list</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  doubly-linked list <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>vector</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  dynamic contiguous array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/inplace_vector\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>inplace_vector</span></span></a></div><div><span class=\"t-lines\"><span><span class=\"t-mark-rev t-since-cxx26\">(C++26)</span></span></span></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  dynamically-resizable, fixed capacity, inplace contiguous array <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/map\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>map</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  collection of key-value pairs, sorted by keys, keys are unique <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/multimap\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>multimap</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  collection of key-value pairs, sorted by keys <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/set\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>set</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  collection of unique keys, sorted by keys <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n<tr class=\"t-dsc\">\n<td>  <div class=\"t-dsc-member-div\"><div><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/multiset\"> <span class=\"t-lines\"><span>multiset</span></span></a></div></div>\n</td>\n<td>  collection of keys, sorted by keys <br> <span class=\"t-mark\">(class template)</span> </td></tr>\n</table>\n<h3 id=\"Example\">Example</h3>\n<div class=\"t-example\"><p>The following example iterates over a <span class=\"t-lc\"><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector\">vector</a></span> (which has <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector#Member_types\">legacy random-access iterators</a>) in reverse.</p>\n<pre data-lang=\"cpp\"><code><span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;iostream&gt;</span>\n<span class=\"co2\">#include &lt;vector&gt;</span>\n&nbsp;\n<span class=\"kw4\">int</span> main<span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">{</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector\"><span class=\"kw1277\">std::<span class=\"me2\">vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span> v <span class=\"sy1\">=</span> <span class=\"br0\">{</span><span class=\"nu0\">3</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">4</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">1</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">5</span>, <span class=\"nu0\">9</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n&nbsp;\n    <span class=\"kw1\">for</span> <span class=\"br0\">(</span><a href=\"/w/cpp/container/vector\"><span class=\"kw1277\">std::<span class=\"me2\">vector</span></span></a><span class=\"sy1\">&lt;</span><span class=\"kw4\">int</span><span class=\"sy1\">&gt;</span><span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">const_reverse_iterator</span> i<span class=\"br0\">{</span>v.<span class=\"me1\">crbegin</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"br0\">}</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> i <span class=\"sy3\">!</span><span class=\"sy1\">=</span> v.<span class=\"me1\">crend</span><span class=\"br0\">(</span><span class=\"br0\">)</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">++</span>i<span class=\"br0\">)</span>\n        <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"sy2\">*</span>i <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">' '</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n    <a href=\"/w/cpp/io/cout\"><span class=\"kw1775\">std::<span class=\"me2\">cout</span></span></a> <span class=\"sy1\">&lt;&lt;</span> <span class=\"st0\">'<span class=\"es1\">\\n</span>'</span><span class=\"sy4\">;</span>\n<span class=\"br0\">}</span></code></pre>\n<p>Output:\n</p>\n<pre data-output=\"1\"><code>9 5 1 4 1 3</code></pre> \n</div>\n<h3 id=\"Defect_reports\">Defect reports</h3>\n<p>The following behavior-changing defect reports were applied retroactively to previously published C++ standards.\n</p>\n<table class=\"dsctable\">\n<tr>\n<th>DR\n</th>\n<th>Applied to\n</th>\n<th>Behavior as published\n</th>\n<th>Correct behavior\n</th></tr>\n<tr>\n<td><a class=\"external text\" href=\"https://cplusplus.github.io/LWG/issue2105\" data-external=\"1\">LWG 2105</a>\n</td>\n<td>C++98\n</td>\n<td><span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw1\">typename</span> X<span class=\"sy4\">::</span><span class=\"me2\">const_reverse_iterator</span></span> was<br>required to be an iterator type of value type <span class=\"mw-geshi cpp source-cpp\"><span class=\"kw4\">const</span> T</span>\n</td>\n<td>required to be a constant<br>iterator type of value type <code>T</code>\n</td></tr></table>","headings":[{"depth":3,"text":"Requirements","id":"Requirements"},{"depth":4,"text":"Types","id":"Types"},{"depth":4,"text":"Expressions","id":"Expressions"},{"depth":3,"text":"Library types","id":"Library_types"},{"depth":3,"text":"Example","id":"Example"},{"depth":3,"text":"Defect reports","id":"Defect_reports"}],"breadcrumbs":[{"path":"","title":"C++ reference"},{"path":"named_req","title":"Named Requirements"}],"children":[],"map":{"label":"C++ named requirements: ReversibleContainer","children":[{"label":"Requirements","note":"A type satisfies ReversibleContainer if it satisfies Container, its iterator type belongs to the bidirectional or random access iterator categories and, given…","children":[{"label":"Types"},{"label":"Expressions","note":"The types reverse_iterator and const_reverse_iterator in the following table denote typename X::reverse_iterator and typename X::const_reverse_iterator…"}]},{"label":"Library types","note":"The following standard library types satisfy ReversibleContainer requirements:","children":[{"label":"array","note":"fixed-sized inplace contiguous array"},{"label":"deque","note":"double-ended queue"},{"label":"list","note":"doubly-linked list"},{"label":"vector","note":"dynamic contiguous array"},{"label":"inplace_vector","note":"dynamically-resizable, fixed capacity, inplace contiguous array"},{"label":"map","note":"collection of key-value pairs, sorted by keys, keys are unique"},{"label":"multimap","note":"collection of key-value pairs, sorted by keys"},{"label":"+2 more"}]},{"label":"Example","note":"The following example iterates over a vector (which has legacy random-access iterators) in reverse."}]},"standards":["C++11","C++26"],"wordCount":346,"codeBlockCount":2}
